{"baseRefName":"dev","body":"[A171]\n\n## Status\n\nComplete local validation at `df53dfa116b34816db0193230ad9833e67bf46dd`, tree `fb7bbe66e6326d9d55b4ad13170446dff12a133a`. Independent reviews and CI remain pending.\n\n## Linked Issue / roles\n\nCloses #423\n\nExecutor A171; manager A10; R243 internal Codex and R244 external Opus.\n\n## Description\n\nAn exact replay containing one redundant merge previously fell through to STRANDED. The final fallback proves the selected merge shape and distinct whitespace-exact historical replay, then requires raw current retention. A permitted three-way merge must return the exact tip bytes; unresolved overlap reports UNKNOWN with the unproved paths.\n\nExisting arm order and linear historical policy remain unchanged. Shared Git transport preserves CRLF and undecodable bytes. The default self-test records 326 assertions, preserving the original 145; public histories, ten guard mutations and boundary cases exercise the new proof. Actual gPTP processor PR62 and the published adjacent extension remain UNKNOWN/nonzero. Repeated-block coverage is bounded and is not a general alignment or semantic-equivalence proof. Separate #514 owns the linear retention-policy decision.\n\n## Authoritative references\n\nREQ-VER-04; CONTRIBUTING section2.1 step7; #423 settled decision5777210218; related #514.\n\n## How to get into the same state\n\nCheckout `df53dfa116b34816db0193230ad9833e67bf46dd` and initialize `third_party/verilog-axis`, `protocol-processor` and `gptp-processor`. Use Verilator 5.050.\n\n## How to validate\n\n```sh\npython3 scripts/check_merge_containment.py --selftest\npython3 scripts/docs_check.py\npython3 scripts/check_py_idiom.py\n```\n\nExpected exit 0. The complete 46+5 local results and exact commands are in the evidence comment. [Author evidence and attribution limits](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/423).\n\n## Known limitations / out of scope\n\nNo hardware campaign, processor-pin adoption, or broader product-compliance claim. Author-only measurements keep their original commit identity; the manager packet separately identifies the tested integration tree.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- [x] Complete local source bar and final source tree integrity\n- [ ] Independent internal and external positive reviews, all five lenses clean\n- [ ] Final-head local replica and required hosted contexts\n- [ ] No outstanding finding or review; current candidate verified\n- [ ] Authorized merge, containment, post-merge hosted checks and Closed/Done\n","commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-09-22T14:15:13Z","authors":[{"email":"hackerman-kl@kebag-logic.com","id":"U_kgDOCaGBZA","login":"Mister-M-alt","name":"hackerman-kl"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-22T14:15:13Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Prove retained replay across one exact redundant merge","oid":"fed4f63f33e6185e5c7e4735a27234db99651d24"},{"authoredDate":"2026-09-22T14:28:03Z","authors":[{"email":"hackerman-kl@kebag-logic.com","id":"U_kgDOCaGBZA","login":"Mister-M-alt","name":"hackerman-kl"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-22T14:28:03Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Validate issue423 candidate against merged PR513","oid":"df53dfa116b34816db0193230ad9833e67bf46dd"}],"files":[{"path":"CONTRIBUTING.md","additions":44,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"scripts/check_merge_containment.py","additions":33,"deletions":33,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"scripts/merge_containment_replay.py","additions":158,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"scripts/merge_containment_selftest.py","additions":4,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"scripts/merge_containment_selftest_mutations.py","additions":66,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"scripts/merge_containment_selftest_replay.py","additions":592,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"scripts/merge_containment_selftest_retention.py","additions":258,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"}],"headRefName":"423-retained-redundant-replay","headRefOid":"df53dfa116b34816db0193230ad9833e67bf46dd","isDraft":false,"state":"OPEN","title":"Prove retained replay across one exact redundant merge","url":"https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/pull/519"}
